[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! The three conversions (`%llx` of the raw bit pattern, glibc's `%a` hexadecimal
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! float form, and `%.4f`) plus glibc's `scanf("%lf")` input grammar are all
